\@writefile{loa}{\contentsline {algorithm}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Algorithm for distributing mass from material parcels, $\Omega ^{n}_{m,i}$ at time $t=t^{n}$ to parcels at $t=t^{n+1}$, $\Omega ^{n+1}_{m,k}$. $m$ is the material id, $i$ is the old parcel id, and $k$ is the new parcel id.  }}{18}{algorithm.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{mass_correction}{{10}{18}{Time step stability restrictions}{algorithm.10}{}}
\@writefile{loa}{\contentsline {algorithm}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Algorithm for adjusting the actual mass, $m^{act}$, of material parcels, $\Omega _{m,k}^{n+1}$, with the parcel's reference mass $m^{ref}$.  }}{18}{algorithm.10}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  The material volume fractions, $F_{m}$, level set functions, $\phi _{m}$, and total energy, $E_{m}$, are stored at cell centers and then consistently interpolated to the refined grid in preparation for Cell Integrated Semi-Lagrangian advection\cite  {jemison2014compressible,scardovelli2003interface}. The velocity $(u,v)$ is piecewise constant interpolated from the face centered (MAC grid) control volumes to the refined grid cell centers. The horizontal advective velocity, $u^{advect}$, is linearly interpolated to the refined grid face centers in the horizontal direction and is piecewise constant interpolated in the vertical direction. The vertical advective velocity, $v^{advect}$, is linearly interpolated in the vertical direction and piecewise constant interpolated in the horizontal direction. The material density $\rho _{m}$ and deviatoric stress tensor components, $s_{m}^{xx,xy,yy,\Theta \Theta }$ (RZ), are already discretized on the refined grid. }}{19}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{prolongation}{{2}{19}{The material volume fractions, $F_{m}$, level set functions, $\phi _{m}$, and total energy, $E_{m}$, are stored at cell centers and then consistently interpolated to the refined grid in preparation for Cell Integrated Semi-Lagrangian advection\cite {jemison2014compressible,scardovelli2003interface}. The velocity $(u,v)$ is piecewise constant interpolated from the face centered (MAC grid) control volumes to the refined grid cell centers. The horizontal advective velocity, $u^{advect}$, is linearly interpolated to the refined grid face centers in the horizontal direction and is piecewise constant interpolated in the vertical direction. The vertical advective velocity, $v^{advect}$, is linearly interpolated in the vertical direction and piecewise constant interpolated in the horizontal direction. The material density $\rho _{m}$ and deviatoric stress tensor components, $s_{m}^{xx,xy,yy,\Theta \Theta }$ (RZ), are already discretized on the refined grid}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces  After Cell Integrated Semi-Lagrangian advection\cite  {jemison2014compressible,scardovelli2003interface} on the refined grid, the cell centered variables, $F_{m}$, $\phi _{m}$, and $E_{m}$, and the face centered variables, $(u,v)$, are conservatively ``recombined'' back to their respective control voume locations. The deviatoric stress tensor components, $s_{m}^{xx,yy,\Theta \Theta }$ (RZ), are conservatively recombined to the cell centered control volumes, and then piecewise constant prolongated back to the refined grid. The off-diagonal deviatoric stress tensor component, $s_{xy}$, is conservatively recombined to the node control volume (RZ) (edge centers in 3D), and then piecewise constant prolongated back to the refined grid. The material density, $\rho _{m}$, do not need to be recombined. }}{20}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{recombination}{{3}{20}{After Cell Integrated Semi-Lagrangian advection\cite {jemison2014compressible,scardovelli2003interface} on the refined grid, the cell centered variables, $F_{m}$, $\phi _{m}$, and $E_{m}$, and the face centered variables, $(u,v)$, are conservatively ``recombined'' back to their respective control voume locations. The deviatoric stress tensor components, $s_{m}^{xx,yy,\Theta \Theta }$ (RZ), are conservatively recombined to the cell centered control volumes, and then piecewise constant prolongated back to the refined grid. The off-diagonal deviatoric stress tensor component, $s_{xy}$, is conservatively recombined to the node control volume (RZ) (edge centers in 3D), and then piecewise constant prolongated back to the refined grid. The material density, $\rho _{m}$, do not need to be recombined}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The phase change algorithm: (1) the phase change speed, $|\dot  {m}|/\rho $, is approximated at all narrow band cells by evaluating $|\dot  {m}|/\rho $ at the corresponding closest point on the interface ($\Gamma ^{n}$). (2) The change in volume fraction due to unsplit CISL advection determines the overall mass correction, $M_{cor}$, due to expansion or compression, $M_{cor}=\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ (F_{dest}^{new}-F_{dest}^{old})V_{grid}(\rho _{m_{s}}-\rho _{m_{d}})$. $M_{cor}$ becomes a source term for the projection step if the material is incompressible, or directly increments the density if the material is compressible. (3) $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the vapor (destination) side of the $\Gamma ^{n+1}$ interface if the interface speed is $\vec  {u}_{m_{s}}+\frac  {|\dot  {m}|}{\rho _{m_{s}}}\vec  {n}_{\Gamma }$ , and $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the liquid (source) side of the interface if the interface speed is $\vec  {u}_{m_{d}}+\frac  {|\dot  {m}|}{\rho _{m_{d}}}\vec  {n}_{\Gamma }$. Referring to the diagram, if distributing $M_{cor}$ to the vapor side, $M_{cor}$ must be all distributed beyond the blue region into the red region.  }}{21}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{mdotproblem}{{4}{21}{The phase change algorithm: (1) the phase change speed, $|\dot {m}|/\rho $, is approximated at all narrow band cells by evaluating $|\dot {m}|/\rho $ at the corresponding closest point on the interface ($\Gamma ^{n}$). (2) The change in volume fraction due to unsplit CISL advection determines the overall mass correction, $M_{cor}$, due to expansion or compression, $M_{cor}=\sum (F_{dest}^{new}-F_{dest}^{old})V_{grid}(\rho _{m_{s}}-\rho _{m_{d}})$. $M_{cor}$ becomes a source term for the projection step if the material is incompressible, or directly increments the density if the material is compressible. (3) $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the vapor (destination) side of the $\Gamma ^{n+1}$ interface if the interface speed is $\vec {u}_{m_{s}}+\frac {|\dot {m}|}{\rho _{m_{s}}}\vec {n}_{\Gamma }$ , and $M_{cor}$ is distributed to the liquid (source) side of the interface if the interface speed is $\vec {u}_{m_{d}}+\frac {|\dot {m}|}{\rho _{m_{d}}}\vec {n}_{\Gamma }$. Referring to the diagram, if distributing $M_{cor}$ to the vapor side, $M_{cor}$ must be all distributed beyond the blue region into the red region}{figure.4}{}}
